  "strategy": "We are to minimize the sequence objective: J(a) = 2 * n * max_k (convolve(a, a)[k]) / sum(a)^2.\n\nApproach and rationale:\n1. We need to avoid being stuck in local optima, so we design an interleaved algorithm of simulated annealing and multiplicative projection over simplex.\n2. We interpret the minimization problem as a searching for sparse distributions with reduced maximum convolution value.\n3. We use multiplicative updates on the simplex structure to avoid oscillations and ensure convergence to a non-negative valid sequence.\n\nMathematical specification:\n- Variables: a = sequence of non-negative floats, length n = 2048.\n- Objective: minimize J(a) = 2*n*M/(s^2) where M = max(convolve(a, a)), s = sum(a).\n- Constraints: a_i >= 0 for all i, and s >= 0.01 (handled by projection).\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Initialization: Start with a normalized bimodal sequence of length 2048, with two peaks at positions of low and high convolution contribution.\n2. Iterative refinement:\n   a) Variance preservation in convolution space.\n   b) Multiplicative update rule to update all coefficients simultaneously.\n3. For each step:\n   a) Randomly select a subset of active coordinates to preserve (90%) and disturb the rest (10%).\n   b) Use simplex projection to maintain probability distribution.\n   c) Compute the next candidate using the current sequence and selection.\n4. Termination criteria:\n   a) 1800 seconds or up.\n   b) Recognize an improvement plateau.\n\nSearch choices and useful variations:\n- Start with bimodal: centers at the first 20% and last 20% of the length.\n- Active coordinates are those contributing in the high convolution area (middle to high peaks).\n- Update strength (temperature) is set to 0.05.\n\nBudget and planning:\n- Allocate 100 seconds for initialization.\n- Each major step (coord descent update) takes 10 seconds, allowing for 170 steps.\n\nValidation and return contract:\n- Compare every candidate with stored best by exact evaluate_sequence call.\n- Return the best sequence found after completing all iterations.",
